---
/**
 * The home's narrative thread: one long, isotype-like hand-drawn line that
 * runs behind the content from the clients strip to the closing CTA and is
 * "drawn" as you scroll (clip-path on a view() timeline, motion.css).
 * Purely decorative. The parent must be `relative isolate`; sections put
 * their content at `z-[2]` so the line passes under cards and text but over
 * section backgrounds. Without timeline support or with reduced motion the
 * line is simply shown complete.
 *
 * The path is one natural cubic spline (continuous curvature, no kinks at
 * the joins). The viewBox is roughly the wrapper's real aspect on desktop
 * (about 1:4) so the non-uniform stretch does not distort the curves.
 * Hidden below `lg`: the gutters are too narrow there and the line would
 * cross the text.
 */
---

<svg
  viewBox="0 0 240 1000"
  preserveAspectRatio="none"
  fill="none"
  aria-hidden="true"
  focusable="false"
  class="scroll-thread pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 z-[1] hidden h-full w-full text-brand opacity-25 lg:block dark:opacity-35"
>
  <path
    stroke="currentColor"
    stroke-width="2"
    stroke-linecap="round"
    vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke"
    d="M216 0 C185.5 26.5 155 53 158.4 88 C161.9 123.6 200.7 168.1 187.2 192 C169.5 223.4 61.7 219.5 43.2 250 C31.2 269.7 56.4 303.7 52.8 336 C49.1 368.9 15.6 399.9 19.2 418 C24.8 446.4 121.2 443 168 480 C199.2 504.7 208.3 547.4 187.2 572 C156.6 607.6 62.8 605 48 638 C37.4 661.6 67.3 703.3 57.6 736 C48.7 766 6.5 788.5 4.8 806 C2.2 831.9 87.6 847 134.4 876 C170.6 898.5 183.7 929.2 196.8 960"
  ></path>
</svg>
